WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:02.970
Instructor: Next up a very quick one: Deleting tags.

00:02.970 --> 00:05.640
We just use the -d flag,

00:05.640 --> 00:07.830
just like with deleting a branch,

00:07.830 --> 00:10.530
and then the tag name that we're referencing.

00:10.530 --> 00:13.983
So let's see. Which one should we delete?

00:15.120 --> 00:19.140
We've got this tag v17.1.0.

00:19.140 --> 00:20.370
Let's do something more obvious.

00:20.370 --> 00:23.580
Let's actually add another tag just where we are right now,

00:23.580 --> 00:25.563
git tag deleteme.

00:27.120 --> 00:29.970
All right, so now if we look at our git log,

00:29.970 --> 00:32.430
we have two tags referring to this commit.

00:32.430 --> 00:34.110
I wanna delete this one.

00:34.110 --> 00:37.290
I can do git tag -d for delete,

00:37.290 --> 00:38.763
and then deleteme,

00:40.470 --> 00:42.360
and it deletes that tag for me.

00:42.360 --> 00:43.920
And if we look at our log again,

00:43.920 --> 00:45.660
we still have that other tag,

00:45.660 --> 00:48.660
but our deleteme tag is completely gone.

00:48.660 --> 00:50.460
So that's all there is to deleting tags.

00:50.460 --> 00:51.360
Nice and easy.
